      "answer": "$T=10\\sqrt2\\,\\mathrm{N}$ (or $14.1\\,\\mathrm{N}$) and $m=\\sqrt3+1\\,\\mathrm{kg}$ (or $2.73\\,\\mathrm{kg}$).",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "$20\\cos60^\\circ=T\\cos45^\\circ$ — M1. Guidance: Resolve forces horizontally, 2 terms.\n$T=10\\sqrt2$ or $T=14.1$ — A1.\n$20\\sin60^\\circ+T\\sin45^\\circ=mg$ or $W$ — M1. Guidance: Resolve forces vertically, 3 terms.\n$20\\sin60^\\circ+T\\sin45^\\circ=mg$ — A1.\n$m=2.73$ [$=\\sqrt3+1$] — A1.\nAlternative method for question 3 (Lami’s method): Attempt at one pair of terms using $\\frac{T}{\\sin150^\\circ}=\\frac{mg\\text{ or }W}{\\sin75^\\circ}=\\frac{20}{\\sin135^\\circ}$ — M1.\n$\\frac{T}{\\sin150^\\circ}=\\frac{mg}{\\sin75^\\circ}=\\frac{20}{\\sin135^\\circ}$ — A1. Guidance: All terms correct in Lami’s Method.\nAttempt to solve for either $T$ or $m$ or $W$ — M1.\n$T=10\\sqrt2$ or $T=14.1$ — A1.\n$m=2.73$ [$=\\sqrt3+1$] — A1.\nAlternative method for question 3 (triangle of forces): Attempt the triangle of forces method and state one equation involving any two of $T$, $m$ and $20$, using $\\frac{T}{\\sin30^\\circ}=\\frac{mg\\text{ or }W}{\\sin105^\\circ}=\\frac{20}{\\sin45^\\circ}$ — M1.\n$\\frac{T}{\\sin30^\\circ}=\\frac{mg}{\\sin105^\\circ}=\\frac{20}{\\sin45^\\circ}$ — A1. Guidance: All correct.\nAttempt to solve for either $T$ or $m$ or $W$ — M1.\n$T=10\\sqrt2$ or $T=14.1$ — A1.\n$m=2.73$ [$=\\sqrt3+1$] — A1.\nTotal: 5.",
